Here is the commit message:
db-fix: resolve crash on fundchannel

Fixes error introduced by 1dbdc74bc where a new fundchannel
can cause a crash after start if the max dbid is for a closed
channel.

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the handling of the maximum database ID (`max_channel_dbid`) when a new channel was created after a restart. If the maximum ID corresponded to a closed channel, it could lead to a crash when attempting to create a new fund channel, as the system did not properly account for the state of closed channels during the initialization process. The changes made ensure that only non-closed channels are loaded and that the maximum ID is set correctly before any new channels are created.

Here is the patch:

-bool wallet_channels_load_active(struct wallet *w)
+static void set_max_channel_dbid(struct wallet *w)
